sequenceDiagram
    participant R1 as Request 1
    participant R2 as Request 2
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    R1->>DB: BEGIN
    R2->>DB: BEGIN

    R1->>DB: SELECT available_seats, version (= 1, 0)
    R2->>DB: SELECT available_seats, version (= 1, 0)

    R1->>DB: UPDATE ... WHERE version = 0 (rowsUpdated = 1)
    R1->>DB: INSERT INTO bookings
    R1->>DB: COMMIT (version is now 1)

    R2->>DB: UPDATE ... WHERE version = 0 (rowsUpdated = 0)
    Note over R2,DB: Version has changed — WHERE clause<br/>does not match
    R2->>DB: ROLLBACK
    Note over R2: Retry (up to 3 times)<br/>then NoSeatsAvailableException
